sequenceDiagram
    participant C as Client
    participant A as Auctions - AuctionEndpoints + CreateAuctionCommandHandler
    participant ADB as Auctions tables
    participant AOP as Auctions OutboxProcessor
    participant I as Inventory - ItemLockRequestedEventHandler
    participant IDB as Inventory tables
    participant IOP as Inventory OutboxProcessor
    participant L as Auctions - ItemLockedEventHandler / ItemLockRejectedEventHandler

    C->>A: POST /api/auctions {itemId, startingPrice, endsOn} with a JWT
    A->>A: ValidationBehaviour, then Auction.Create with Status = Pending
    A->>ADB: INSERT Auctions + OutboxMessages(ItemLockRequestedEvent) in one SaveChangesAsync
    A-->>C: 201 {publicAuctionId}
    AOP->>ADB: every 3 s: due outbox rows, max 20
    AOP->>I: IIntegrationEventPublisher, MediatR Publish(ItemLockRequestedEvent)
    I->>IDB: WasEventProcessedAsync(EventId)
    I->>I: GetUserItemAsync(SellerUserId, PublicItemId), Item.LockForAuction(PublicAuctionId)
    I->>IDB: UPDATE InventoryItems + InventoryProcessedMessages + InventoryOutboxMessages(reply) in one SaveChangesAsync
    IOP->>L: Publish(ItemLockedEvent or ItemLockRejectedEvent) on the next Inventory poll
    alt ItemLockedEvent
        L->>ADB: Auction.Activate(ItemName, ItemRarity, OfficialPrice) + AuctionsProcessedMessages + OutboxMessages(AuctionActivatedEvent)
    else ItemLockRejectedEvent
        L->>ADB: Auction.Cancel(Reason) + AuctionsProcessedMessages
    end
    Note over AOP,IOP: creation to activation takes up to two polling cycles of 3 s each
